<title>PORTUGAL: Vidago shares to resume trade in Lisbon 1100 GMT.</title>
<headline>Vidago shares to resume trade in Lisbon 1100 GMT.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Portuguese mineral water firm Vidago will resume trade on Lisbon bourse at 1100 GMT after trade in the shares was suspended on Monday, a bourse spokesman said.</p>
<p>Earlier on Friday the bourse lifted a suspension in the trade of shares in retailer Jeronimo Martins.</p>
<p>Jeronimo Martins &amp; Filho-SGPS issued a statement on Thursday saying it was studying the possibility of launching a public offer to buy Vidago.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +351-1-3538254  </p>
